# Line endings.
#
# Git for Windows ships core.autocrlf=true in its *system* config (not this
# repo, not the global file), so a checkout here produced CRLF working-tree
# files while the index stayed LF. gofmt requires LF and treats a CRLF file as
# unformatted, so `gofmt -l ./...` in palabatu-be reported 69 of 74 Go files as
# needing formatting purely because of line endings, which makes it useless as
# a real formatting check. Same class of noise for any other tool that reads
# the working tree rather than the index.
#
# These rules override core.autocrlf per path, so every clone on every machine
# checks out LF regardless of local git config. Do not "fix" a CRLF complaint
# by editing files or changing core.autocrlf -- change it here.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts. Run by powershell.exe/cmd.exe and by nothing in the Go
# or Node toolchains, so they keep the platform convention.
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never diffed or line-ending-converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
